  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 21 May 1952 and declared by Geo. McGowan, returning officer, on Thursday 22 May. The three aldermen elected in 1947 and all twelve councillors were due for election. Labels as printed: Offl. U. official Unionist, U Unionist, Ex-Ser. ex-serviceman, Trades C. Mid-Ulster Trades Council. Aldermen: A. L. Martin, the official Unionist candidate, topped the poll with a record 3,081; 4,545 votes were cast in a 57 per cent poll, with 256 spoilt (149 unmarked). Cassells, an alderman since 1947, lost his seat."
